{
  "description": "Standalone database server signatures for host-native auto-discovery on Linux. Only daemons that run with their own PID, own port/socket, and own data directory are included. Matching priority: executables (primary) > cmdline_tokens (secondary, required for generic runtimes like java/beam.smp) > fd_signatures (tertiary, process must have file open at runtime). binary_strings are ONLY used for generic-runtime databases (java, beam.smp) where the executable alone is insufficient — they must be internal class/module names that only the server process loads, not product names that appear in client drivers or dependencies. All entries include config_location and config_rules for write_path/data_dir extraction. Removed: embedded databases (SQLite, LevelDB, RocksDB, DuckDB, Chroma), monitoring-category databases (Prometheus — covered in monitoring_signatures), messaging-category (NATS — covered in mq_signatures), duplicates (etcd — covered in container_signatures).",

  "databases": [
